    {
      "id": "source-3",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T21:20:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the live Ethereum receipt and complete call trace, the two victim architectures and pre-exploit hashes, NFTLiquidationProxy creation and every pre-exploit NewImplementation event, custom implementation storage slot 2, oETH creation and immutable runtime, explorer-verified source, the commit-pinned reproduction, exact token transfers, and published technical reporting. The seed row's target incorrectly treated implementation 0xf10bc5be84640236c71173d1809038af4ee19002 as a direct execution address; the exploit actually calls proxy 0x323398de3c35f96053d930d25fe8d92132f83d44, which delegates the vulnerable liquidateWithSingleRepay calls to that artifact. Its sole NewImplementation event selected the artifact at 16727653:52 log 78 and slot 2 retained it through the exploit. Separately, direct oETH 0x2ccb7d00a9e10d0c3408b5eefb67011abfacb075 executes the empty-market donation and rounding loop. The two defects compose: fake repay and collateral oTokens control the liquidation path and reenter a real liquidation after oETH's exchange rate has been manipulated. The receipt establishes the exact VUSD, XCN, DAI, WBTC and USDT components; security reporting values the gross basket at approximately $3.8 million."
